      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Western Ridge, Barossa Valley",
        "heading": "A village shaped by welcome.",
        "body": "<p>The estate sits among the westerly townships of Seppeltsfield, Greenock and Marananga, where rolling vineyard hills meet open fields of cereal crops.</p><p>More than 2,000 Canary Island Date Palms line the approaching roads as an avenue to the property. Upon arrival, a Barossa community of wine, food, art and beauty awaits: Cellar Door, FINO, JamFactory and the wider village.</p><p>Throughout the 19th and 20th centuries, the Seppelt family were known for generous hospitality, welcoming travellers of all origins. We continue that village vision, sharing the history, heritage and provenance of this remarkable estate.</p>",
