        "section_anchor_id": "vineyards",
        "eyebrow": "Vineyards",
        "heading": "The Great Terraced Vineyard.",
        "body": "<p>Vineyards immediately around the estate span more than 250 acres, planted to the Barossa's traditional varieties of Shiraz, Grenache and Cabernet, with small holdings of Touriga. Wider plantings run across the Western Ridge and into the Eden Valley.</p><p>The most prized site is the Great Terraced Vineyard, on a hillside of ironstone, quartz and slate. Its bush-vine Grenache, 60 to 80 years old, is planted in contours that follow the land. Fruit once reserved for fortified wine now also becomes small-batch still wines.</p>",
        "link_label": "Discover our winemaking",
        "link_url": "/pages/winemaking",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Great_Terraced_Vineyard_Tour.jpg",
        "badge_text": "Bush vine Grenache · 60–80 years",
        "layout": "copy_left",
