        "label_heading": "An unbroken lineage of every vintage since 1878.",
        "eyebrow": "The cellars",
        "heading": "A living museum of Australian wine.",
        "body": "<p>Joseph Seppelt began plans for a new bluestone cellar in 1866. Twelve years later, after his father's death, Benno completed the stone cellars and set aside a puncheon of his finest wine, not to be bottled for 100 years.</p><p>That 1878 Tawny remains the start of an unbroken lineage. Each vintage still lays down a barrel of the finest wine. The Centennial Cellar is a living museum of Australian winemaking, and the jewel in the crown of the estate.</p>",
        "link_label": "Taste it at Cellar Door",
