    "estate_gravity": {
      "type": "sf2-feature-banner",
      "settings": {
        "section_anchor_id": "",
        "eyebrow": "1888 Gravity Cellar",
        "heading": "Built into the hillside. Revived for vintage.",
        "body": "<p>Oscar Benno Seppelt designed the Gravity Cellar as a series of terraces, so fruit could move through the winery by gravity. What began as engineering logic is now a coveted winemaking principle: minimal handling, open fermentation, and wines of heightened aroma and purity.</p><p>Decommissioned in the 1980s and dormant for nearly 30 years, the cellar was revived for the 2010 vintage and is once again at the centre of Seppeltsfield winemaking.</p>",
        "link_label": "Meet the winemaking team",
        "link_url": "/pages/winemaking#team",
